  "content": {
    "id": "p24-q29-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "29",
    "prompt": "The lines $y=mx+6$ and $y=nx-3$ meet at a point where $x=9$. Find the values of $m$ and $n$ if $m+n=7$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$m=3,\\ n=4$.",
      "worked": "At the intersection, both expressions give the same value of $y$. Substituting $x=9$ gives\n$$\\begin{align*}9m+6&=9n-3\\\\9m-9n&=-9\\\\m-n&=-1.\\end{align*}$$\nUsing $m+n=7$, substitute $m=7-n$:\n$$\\begin{align*}7-n-n&=-1\\\\7-2n&=-1\\\\-2n&=-8\\\\n&=4.\\end{align*}$$\nThen\n$$\\begin{align*}m&=7-4\\\\m&=3.\\end{align*}$$\nCheck: $3+4=7$, and at $x=9$ both lines give $y=33$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 64
  },
